ency, and unanimous Safe or Solid Republican ratings from expert raters outweigh a Democratic-leaning national environment; prediction markets price a Masuda upset near one-in-ten, consistent with a Likely Republican race rather than a lock.", "watch": "A strong Democratic wave or late polling showing Masuda competitive in the Central Valley could pull the race toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom McClintock (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Tom McClintock, the Republican incumbent, seeks another term in a Central Valley and Sierra foothill district that leans Republican by roughly ten points; 2026 redistricting doubled the district's size but left the GOP advantage intact. Democrat Michael Masuda, a first-time candidate, has campaigned across the district's smaller towns and earned a Fresno Bee editorial endorsement, but he enters the general election with limited name recognition.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on district fundamentals and outside assessments. Expert raters unanimously place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Masuda roughly a one-in-ten chance. McClintock has out-raised Masuda more than two-to-one and holds the cash advantage. A Democratic-leaning national environment is the strongest factor working in Masuda's favor, but the partisan baseline and incumbency make McClintock the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -9.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1311, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0595, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0545, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0432, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0389,